---
import Base from '../../layouts/Base.astro';
import SectionNav from '../../components/SectionNav.astro';
---
<Base title="Update a page" description="Each public page is a JSON file. The template decides the layout. You fill named fields. You do not invent a new design per city." path="/about/editing">
  <article class="wrap section">
    <h1>Update a page</h1>
    <p>Each public page is a JSON file in <code>src/content</code>. The template decides the layout. You fill named fields. You do not invent a new design per city.</p>
    <SectionNav
      label="Editing sections"
      items={[
        { id: 'direct', label: 'Direct edit' },
        { id: 'agent', label: 'With an agent' },
      ]}
    />
    <div class="reading">
    <section id="direct" class="place-section">
    <h2>Direct edit</h2>
    <p>Open the place file, change the fact, and set <code>verified</code> to the day you checked it. Leave a fee blank of invented numbers. If you do not have a source, write “Check on arrival.”</p>
    </section>
    <section id="agent" class="place-section">
    <h2>With an agent</h2>
    <p>Ask for a draft against the schema in <code>AGENTS.md</code>. The agent shows a diff. You publish by building. Season notes can be added on a place as the <code>season</code> field. Do not rewrite the evergreen intro to sound like today’s weather.</p>
    <p>Run <code>npm run check:content</code> before a build. The build refuses a broken link or a duplicate slug.</p>
    </section>
    </div>
  </article>
</Base>
